 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "«قل» (27:10, 30:18): no plate starts on it, and none on the Prophet's ﷺ words about himself. 27:10-15 keeps Al-Muyassar's «من المعاندين عن الهداية». Geometric for «الله يضل من يشاء», light for «ويهدي إليه من أناب», «تطمئن القلوب… طوبى لهم» (no tree or Paradise drawn) and «الذي أوحينا إليك» (the revelation). STAGING v4: c1 (27) stays ambient: the disbelievers' demand for a sign on the Prophet ﷺ (their behaviour toward him) and his commanded answer («قل», quiet over 27:10-19); geometric for Allah leaves astray whom He wills; the light plate now starts on whoever turns to Him (27:18), not on His act of guiding. c2 (28-29): three believers sit in a prayer hall by day; a light plate and a soft sparkle for hearts at rest in the remembrance of Allah (28:3-10; nothing is read: the tafsirs give remembrance, and As-Sa'di the Book only as a second view); for those who believe and do righteous deeds they stand and pray (29:2-8: standing, bowing, rising, prostrating, sitting; As-Sa'di names the prayer among the deeds of the limbs), facing the empty side of the hall; plates fade while they pray. Nothing of Paradise is drawn for the good return. c3 (30) stays ambient: Allah's words to the Prophet ﷺ about his mission and his commanded words (quiet over all of 30); the light plate for what We revealed to you is now a book plate (no light starting near His act of revealing)."
 },
